course: dictionary
lesson: 9683
title: Context clues: suet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word, and they often give you clues to its meaning. In the list «suet» = hard fat used in cooking, the = sign tells you the meaning straight away.
explain: Suet is a hard, white fat. It comes from around the kidneys of cows and sheep. Cooks use it to make dumplings, Christmas pudding and mince pies.
explain: Vegetable suet is a similar fat, but it is made from plants. Bird lovers also put suet balls out in winter to feed the birds.
fact: Suet is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some suet, not two suets.
fact: «Suet» means hard fat from around the kidneys of cows and sheep, used in cooking.
fact: «Vegetable suet» means a similar fat made from plants.
fact: In British and Irish cooking, suet makes dumplings, Christmas pudding, mince pies and steamed puddings.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows and other old stories, suet puddings are hearty country food.
exercise: Old words in today's English: «suet» = hard fat used in cooking. What is suet? | Thin clear liquid for drinking | *Hard fat used in cooking | Soft sweet sugar for cakes | Dried leaves for making tea
exercise: Suet is used in British and Irish cooking to make what? | *Dumplings | Glass windows | Rain clouds | Paper bags
exercise: Vegetable suet is a similar fat made from what? | *Plants | Cows' kidneys | Bricks | Sea water
test: Why do bird lovers put suet balls out in winter? | To make the garden smell nice | To keep cats away | *To feed the birds | To make bread rise
test: Hard white fat from around the kidneys of cows and sheep is called what? | Marzipan | Gravy | *Suet | Yeast
exam: In The Wind in the Willows, suet puddings are described as what kind of food? | Fancy restaurant food | Plastic food | Food from outer space | *Hearty country food
